Ray had 25 lollipops. He kept 5 lollipops for himself. This means he had 25 - 5 = 20 lollipops to share. He shared these 20 lollipops equally with his four friends. To find out how many lollipops each friend received, we divide the number of lollipops to share (20) by the number of friends (4). So, 20 / 4 = 5.

Each of his friends received 5 lollipops.

